# Prompts

Import ProblemRecord from "./problem_record.lg".
Import AttemptRecord from "./attempt_record.lg".
Import WorkRecord from "./work_record.lg".
Import ChatRequest from "./chat_request.lg".
Import VernacularCommand from "./vernacular_command.lg".
Import PromptTasks from "./prompt_tasks.lg".
Import PromptRoles from "./prompt_roles.lg".
Import Reference from "./reference.lg".

What a model is asked. Every prompt has the same parts in the same place: a
SYSTEM message with the role and the whole kernel reference, and a USER message
with the problem, the accepted statement (when there is one), the trail digest,
the verified lemmas it may cite, the strategy's playbook, the task, and the
answer contract. The playbook and the sampling budget are the strategy's; the
reference, the contract and the acceptance rules are not.

## Note
Everything a prompt draws on; `previous`, `diagnostics` and `failedBlock` are
the last submission, the kernel's error and the refused block, for a repair.

## A PromptContext has:
    a problem, which is Problem.
    a statement, which is Text.
    a goalName, which is Text.
    a trailDigest, which is Text.
    a lemmas, which is Seq of Lemma.
    a playbook, which is Text.
    a previous, which is Text.
    a diagnostics, which is Text.
    a failedBlock, which is Text.

## A Prompt has:
    a kind, which is Text.
    a system, which is Text.
    a user, which is Text.

## Note
The problem as the model reads it.

## To problemSection (p: Problem) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be "## The problem\n\n" + p's id + " — " + p's title + "\nSource: " + p's source + ", collection " + p's collection + ".".
    If p's statementInformal is not equal to "":
        Set out to out + "\n\n" + p's statementInformal.
    Inspect p's leanStatement:
        When Some (lean):
            Return out + "\n\nThe Lean statement:\n\n```lean\n" + lean + "\n```".
        When None:
            Return out + "\n\nThere is no Lean statement of it.".
    Return out.

## Note
The sections after the problem, each only when it has something in it.

## To contextSections (c: PromptContext) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    If c's statement is not equal to "":
        Push "## The statement\n\nThis document is checked first, exactly as written. It defines `" + c's goalName + "`.\n\n```logos-kernel\n" + c's statement + "\n```" to out.
    Push "## What has been tried\n\n" + c's trailDigest to out.
    If length of c's lemmas is greater than 0:
        Let mutable ls be a new Seq of Text.
        Repeat for l in c's lemmas:
            Push "- `" + l's name + "`: " + l's statement to ls.
        Push "## Verified lemmas\n\nThese are proved; to use one, include it in your block under a new name.\n\n" + join(ls, "\n") to out.
    If c's playbook is not equal to "":
        Push "## Playbook\n\n" + c's playbook to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The prompt for a unit of `kind` in context `c`.

## To buildPrompt (kind: Text, c: PromptContext) -> Prompt:
    Let task be taskText(kind, c's goalName, proofNameFor(c's goalName), c's previous, c's failedBlock, c's diagnostics).
    Let user be join([problemSection(c's problem)] + contextSections(c) + [task, contractText(kind)], "\n\n").
    Return a new Prompt with kind kind and system (roleText(kind) + "\n\n" + kernelReference()) and user user.

## Note
A prompt as the request a strategy sends.

## To promptRequest (p: Prompt, s: Strategy) -> ChatRequest:
    Let messages be [a new ChatMessage with role "system" and content p's system, a new ChatMessage with role "user" and content p's user].
    Return a new ChatRequest with model s's model and messages messages and maxTokens s's maxTokens and temperatureBp s's temperatureBp.
